{"title":"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there is a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1bb51afff5fb240f36891f4551733ba8a674630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> with the following property: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4211b2769e07903568a3bb3e0fd9e52a113cf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a28370845df4646c9a8741723cc5beb04c2a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a+i, b+j)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff09116fe0cd1be9000acb1d03cc4599dce45c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, j\\in\\{0, 1, \\ldots n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, then<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b7074a6db67693e1ca47702b4fe57d70147d3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\min\\{a, b\\}&gt;c^n\\cdot n^{\\frac{n}{2}}.\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The following solution is due to Gabriel Dospinescu and v_Enhance (also known as Evan Chen).\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330856c3b7b6bef0dce6f0f10b509e028db40628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is (very) large. We construct an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb21db0177b65427c9c7fb7bd9183d242bdbcb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\times N$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> with cells <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887919dfbc86eebc29e0373f98f97dbf23a0ae23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i,j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2af98bd7a75f3dedad647918dc00415c2b667a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le i, j \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> and in each cell place a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be87a2718ae808bd210d01e72c63b700a4685739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd (a+i, b+j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The central claim is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the primes in this table exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a8f8ba72baaf6335e74c5d27b8bf881ca5a835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.001n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. We count the maximum number of squares they could occupy:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/8526efa4ab4984071741ebe1c341bab60bbda76c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_p \\left\\lceil \\frac{N}{p} \\right\\rceil^2  \t\t\\le \\sum_p \\left( \\frac Np + 1 \\right)^2 \\\\ \t\t= N^2 \\sum_p \\frac{1}{p^2} + 2N \\sum_p \\frac1p + \\sum_p 1.\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"51\" /> Here the summation runs over primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48fb0dec9234658dbaf3a5c7aa67add7464e6f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\le 0.001n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/01537b800d351b3c7ad198bbe28634849113dae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\pi(0.001n^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" /> denote the number of such primes. Now we apply the three bounds: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ed4603fa4f0a1eaec19bce62dc49a5962903d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_p \\frac{1}{p^2} &lt; \\frac 12\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"47\" /> which follows by adding all the primes directly with some computation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6e72d6e93aee716739125f7752be4aeeeb9e45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_p \\frac 1p &lt; \\sum_{k=1}^r \\frac 1k = O(\\ln r) &lt; o(N)\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"49\" /> using the harmonic series bound, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53dc72482811ae3f73269339a30774204dae1ae9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_p 1 &lt; r \\sim O \\left( \\frac{N^2}{\\ln N} \\right) &lt; o(N^2)\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"48\" /> via Prime Number Theorem.  Hence the sum in question is certainly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16ace5af551a043e8558c71e8d862f556b3f6af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac 12 N^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"36\" height=\"23\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> large enough, establishing the central claim.\n</p><p>Hence some column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e2a1a5bc2baaf357faba06745f9399936deeff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> has at least one half of its primes greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a8f8ba72baaf6335e74c5d27b8bf881ca5a835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.001n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. Because this is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, these primes must all be distinct, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e2a1a5bc2baaf357faba06745f9399936deeff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> exceeds their product, which is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f41fdc4a3e28a47399ccc5e8d20b339674ec6c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( 0.001n^2 \\right)^{N/2} &gt; c^n \\cdot n^n\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"26\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is some constant.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155428\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 102/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5380/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12664:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017155428 and revision id 126476. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}